# Third-party benchmark source archives. NEVER committed: the scoped parts are
# vendored extracted instead, under fave/bench/wl_cloud/cloud-tf/ and
# fave/bench/deltanet/traces/, where git reveals any change to them. The cloud
# archive is not kept at all (owner, 2026-09-18). The Delta-net archive IS kept
# in the checkout root since 2026-09-29 (owner), so that files derived from it
# can be re-derived by script rather than vendored -- which makes this guard
# load-bearing, not just a precaution.
cloud_bench.tar.bz2
deltanet-NSDI17-dataset.tar.gz
nsdi-data-sets/
# Derived from the kept archive, NOT vendored (owner, 2026-09-29): 386 MB,
# re-derived by fave/bench/deltanet/archive_survey/insert_block.sh and pinned
# in traces/DERIVED.SHA256SUMS -- a manifest of its own, because verify_raw
# fails on a listed file that is absent, and a checkout without the archive
# must still verify the vendored airtel traces.
fave/bench/deltanet/traces/berkeley-inserts.csv

